# When working on an app — read both layers

1. `{app}/README.md` + `{app}/docs/` (reusable)
2. `instance/{app}/Readme.md` (this infra instance)
3. Secrets keys only: `instance/{app}/.env` / `.env.oidc`
4. Domains: `instance/caddy/.env`. SMTP: `instance/email/.env`

| Apps | Skills, docs, rules |
|---|---|
| Dockge | `.cursor/skills/agentskillexchange-skills-dockge-docker-compose-stack-manager/SKILL.md` (start/status/get/down). List/update: `truenas-scale/scripts/dockge-*.mjs` |
| n8n | `.agents/skills/using-n8n-skills-official` |
| TrueNAS,n8n,NocoDB,Dockge | `.cursor/skills/truenas-scale/SKILL.md` & `.cursor/mcp.json` · `instance/truenas/Readme.md` |
| Authentik | `.cursor/skills/authentik/SKILL.md` (always; run `scripts/`, never ad-hoc API) · `instance/authentik/Readme.md` |
| WordPress | `.agents/skills/wordpress-pro/SKILL.md`, `.agents/skills/wp-plugin-directory-guidelines/SKILL.md` |
| FileFlows | `.agents/skills/fileflow-pathologize` |
| find-skills | Discover/install skills from [skills.sh](https://skills.sh/). Search: `npx skills find [query]`. Add: `npx skills add owner/repo --skill name -y` (omit `-g` = this repo) |
| Proxmox | `proxmox/MCP.md` · `instance/proxmox/Readme.md` |

• Preffer not to create temporary docker containers, when working on Dockge stacks
but if you did it (or script does this) - remove temp containers when you done
For example: applying Nextcloud mail configuration; after configuration applied - remove this temporary docker container
(if couldnt, dont nuke; just tell the user)

